<title>USA: NEC seeks dumping investigation suspension.</title>
<headline>NEC seeks dumping investigation suspension.</headline>
<dateline>BOXBOROUGH, Mass. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>NEC Corp said that it and its U.S. subsidiary, HNSX Supercomputers Inc, on Tuesday asked a federal court to suspend a Commerce Department antidumping investigation involving NEC supercomputers.</p>
<p>The investigation began after Cray Computer Corp accused NEC of dumping - or selling at deep discounts to achieve market share - supercomputing equipment in the U.S.</p>
<p>NEC said it filed a suit in the Court of International Trade in New York alleging that Commerce officials prejudged the merits of Cray's allegations before the dumping investigation was initiated.</p>
</text>
